# Local run config: contains live credentials, must never be committed.
# ROOT-ANCHORED, and it matters: a bare `config/` has no leading slash, so git
# matches a directory of that name at ANY depth -- which silently ignored the
# whole `src/main/scala/kotllm/config` source package. Files already tracked
# kept working, so the only symptom was a new file in that package vanishing
# from `git add` without a word. SessionStore.scala nearly shipped that way.
/config/
history.txt

# The Python session's virtual environment, created on first use of
# python_eval. Tens to hundreds of MB, and entirely reproducible.
pyenv/

